{
  "id": "plural",
  "name": "Plurals of nouns and adjectives",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "fr-FR",
  "subtitle": "In writing, add -s: une maison → des maisons. Words in -eau and -eu add -x (un gâteau → des gâteaux), and words in -al change to -aux (un journal → des journaux). The -s is silent, so in speech the article les or des shows the plural.",
  "briefMarks": ["-s", "-x", "-aux", "les", "des"],
  "source": "icanspeak French original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-08)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "les / des", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "noun + -s / -x", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "adjective + -s", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "maison → maison<span class=\"vp-verb\">s</span> · gâteau → gâteau<span class=\"vp-verb\">x</span> · journal → journ<span class=\"vp-verb\">aux</span> · la voiture rouge → <span class=\"vp-prep\">les</span> voiture<span class=\"vp-verb\">s</span> rouge<span class=\"vp-verb\">s</span>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Most nouns add <strong>-s</strong>: <em>un livre → des livres, une rue → des rues</em>. You don't hear the -s. You hear the plural in the article: <em>le livre</em> but <em>les livres</em>.",
        "tag": "Add -s"
      },
      {
        "html": "Nouns in <strong>-eau</strong> and <strong>-eu</strong> add <strong>-x</strong>: <em>un gâteau → des gâteaux, un bureau → des bureaux, un jeu → des jeux</em>.",
        "tag": "-eau, -eu: -x"
      },
      {
        "html": "Nouns in <strong>-al</strong> change to <strong>-aux</strong>: <em>un journal → des journaux, un animal → des animaux, un hôpital → des hôpitaux</em>.",
        "tag": "-al: -aux"
      },
      {
        "html": "Nouns that end in <strong>-s, -x, -z</strong> do not change. Only the article shows the plural: <em>le prix → les prix, un fils → des fils, le nez → les nez</em>.",
        "tag": "No change"
      },
      {
        "html": "A few plurals are irregular: <em>un œil → des yeux</em>. Learn them as they come.",
        "tag": "Irregular"
      },
      {
        "html": "Everything around the noun changes too: <em>la petite maison blanche → les petites maisons blanches</em>. A group of men and women takes the masculine: <em>des voisins</em> can be men and women.",
        "tag": "Agreement"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>des journals</em> → ✓ <em>des journaux</em>. ✗ <em>les gâteaus</em> → ✓ <em>les gâteaux</em>. ✗ <em>les maison</em> → ✓ <em>les maisons</em>. ✗ <em>des prixs</em> → ✓ <em>des prix</em>. More on adjectives: <a href=\"/accord-des-adjectifs\">Adjectives: agreement and position</a>.",
    "reference": {
